  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Complex <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is most stable complex<br />among the given complex compounds because<br />more number of chelate rings are present in this complex as compare to others.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;chelate ring<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;chelate ring<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math> chelate ring<br />(4) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>Co</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>6</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;chelate ring</p>"
